Desktop host on SDL3 instead of raylib: window, presentation, keyboard and gamepads, audio output, debug UI. SDL3 (release-3.4.18, static) and miniz (3.0.2, the raw deflate raylib's CompressData gave game code) are fetched by CMake; imgui gets its own SDL3 and SDL GPU backends in place of rlImGui. include/runtime/ps2_host.h is the host's API: a window placed without focus (PS2X_WINDOW_POS), an SDL GPU device (Direct3D 12 or Vulkan on Windows, Metal on macOS; PS2X_GPU=d3d12|vulkan picks one), the display frame uploaded and blitted at its display aspect with nearest sampling as before, overlay and replacement hooks (the debug UI draws over the frame; a native renderer can draw the whole image), keyboard state by scancode, any gamepad SDL knows (in connection order), and an audio stream pulled by a callback. include/runtime/ps2_host_compat.h keeps the raylib names the pad and audio code was written against (KEY_*, GAMEPAD_*, IsKeyDown, Sound and Wave). The present mode is immediate (else mailbox) without PS2X_VSYNC=1, vsync with it; PS2X_PRESENT=free paces the window loop at 60 Hz by itself, as raylib's frame timer did. The Vita build keeps raylib. Checked in Metropolismania: all 4 MB of VRAM byte-identical to the raylib build at the eleven views of a scripted city camera run (and between two runs); explore autoplay at the same game speed on Direct3D 12 and Vulkan, a frame on its way 8 to 9 ms after the vertical blank on average; 89 s of 48 kHz audio delivered; the debug UI draws over the game.

